## The Radar key

Many accessible toilets are locked to keep them clean and free for the people who need them. A **Radar key** (part of the National Key Scheme) opens **over 10,000** of them across the UK.

- buy a **genuine Radar key** from **Disability Rights UK**, which costs about **£6** at the time of writing
- some councils give them out free or cheaply
- beware of cheap copies online, which may not work

## Changing Places toilets

**Changing Places** toilets are larger than standard accessible toilets and have a **height-adjustable changing bench**, a **hoist**, and space for up to two carers. They are for people who cannot use a standard accessible toilet. Use the **Changing Places map** online to find one near you.

## Cards that can help when you are out

- **Just Can't Wait card:** a free card from the Bladder and Bowel Community that asks shops and businesses to let you use their toilet, for people with bladder or bowel conditions
- **Hidden Disabilities Sunflower lanyard:** shows you may need extra help or time, recognised in many shops, stations and airports
- **"Please offer me a seat" badge:** free from Transport for London for people who find it hard to stand on public transport
